# pipeline_output holds derived products -- rebinned spectra, staged exposures,
# fit figures and their JSON records -- which are regenerated from the archive
# by the scripts in finalrun/ and are far too large to version.  Everything here
# is ignored EXCEPT the hand-authored override tables under final/, which are
# inputs rather than outputs: without them the pipeline runs and quietly
# produces different spectra.
#
# decisions.csv is NOT among them any more.  The ledger's canonical copy is
# Data/decisions.csv; a second copy lived here and went stale twice, sitting at
# 204 rows for three weeks while the real ledger passed 450.  rebin_path.py now
# names the one ledger and every reader imports it, so a copy here would be a
# duplicate with nothing reading it.  Past versions remain in git history.
*
!.gitignore
!final/
final/*
!final/spectrum_overrides.csv
!final/name_overrides.csv
# bal_status.csv is hand-curated too: which adopted objects are BALs, with
# the evidence for each.  Needed to read the Mg II sweep, where a BAL is
# EXPECTED to show the model exceeding the observed line (index 422), so a
# high ratio is a signature rather than a failure.  Text-matching the ledger
# for "BAL" does not reproduce it -- five hits are boilerplate about an
# unreliable test and three are cross-references to other objects.
!final/bal_status.csv
